  "accepted_answers": [
    "1810-11",
    "1798-1800 (West Haven, Vermont)"
  ],
  "explanation": "The question asks when the Simeon Smith House was built. The original sources present multiple distinct referents:\n\n1. **Portsmouth, New Hampshire** - Two documents (D1 and D2) describe a Simeon Smith House in Portsmouth, with conflicting construction dates: 1810-11 (D1) and 1910-11 (D2). These are likely errors or transpositions, but both refer to the same building in Portsmouth. Only the 1810-11 version is retained as it aligns with the historical context of the 1813 fire.\n\n2. **West Haven, Vermont** - Documents D3, D4, and D7 describe a separate Simeon Smith House in West Haven, built in 1798–1800. This is clearly a distinct entity and should be preserved with its location qualifier.\n\nThe 1790s references (C3, C5) pertain to a farmhouse on the Simeon Smith Mansion property (D5-D7), which is a different structure altogether and not the Simeon Smith House itself. It is excluded unless explicitly asked for."
}
